      "Language": "dan",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Periostal avulsion of m. vastus medialis is a very rare injury. To our knowledge, it has not previously been described, and there is no treatment algorithm. A 32-year-old male professional triathlete experienced this type of injury during a final sprint in a competition. He achieved a good functional result after treatment with an optimal rehabilitation regimen, and approximately four months after the injury he won a medal in a major international event."},
